    {
      "day": 2,
      "line": "🐪 A river trader walks into Haven a day early — word of the village's standing travels faster than feet. \"Heard Haven's name on the river,\" they say, pack heavy, smile practiced. \"Thought I'd see it for myself.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 12,
      "line": "Farid leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about The Big Beast. Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 12,
      "line": "💡 COUNTER LEARNED — The Big Beast: Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 17,
      "line": "Riders on the ridge — no, a cart. A TRADER. Word travels: Haven has food, and where there's food there's trade."
    },
    {
      "day": 18,
      "line": "A cart-driver with flour on their sleeves waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
